body:
> This happens because localization information is stored in the project settings (project.godot). When pck is loaded dynamically, the project settings are not updated.

In the MRP, the list of translation files is not changed. So it's not related to information stored in project settings.

No resources will be reloaded in `load_resource_pack()`. This behavior is not limited to translation files.

Force reloading the cache for every file loaded from PCK seems to solve the problem. But it's a core behavior change and I'm not sure if it's intended:

```diff
diff --git i/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp w/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
index 244469e9d9..d10d6e6386 100644
--- i/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
+++ w/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
@@ -323,6 +323,14 @@ bool PackedSourcePCK::try_open_pack(const String &p_path, bool p_replace_files,
 			PackedData::get_singleton()->remove_path(path);
 		} else {
 			PackedData::get_singleton()->add_path(p_path, path, file_base + ofs, size, md5, this, p_replace_files, (flags & PACK_FILE_ENCRYPTED), sparse_bundle);
+
+			if (!path.begins_with("res://")) {
+				path = "res://" + path;
+			}
+			Ref<Resource> res = ResourceCache::get_ref(path.trim_suffix(".import"));
+			if (res.is_valid()) {
+				res->reload_from_file();
+			}
 		}
 	}
```

> With that in mind, maybe there's an argument for doing something similar to what you proposed @timothyqiu but only for *.translation files, since they might fall under this category as well?

Is it always wanted for all translations? Force-reloading all resources is probably not good, but it might be useful for a lot of them. This might be something that can use an extra file flag in the PCK and be configured when patch PCK is created (not sure what's the best UI for this would be).

```diff
diff --git a/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp b/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
index 244469e9d9..75c8135119 100644
--- a/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
+++ b/core/io/file_access_pack.cpp
@@ -305,6 +305,7 @@ bool PackedSourcePCK::try_open_pack(const String &p_path, bool p_replace_files,
                f = fae;
        }

+       Vector<String> resources_to_reload;
        for (int i = 0; i < file_count; i++) {
                uint32_t sl = f->get_32();
                CharString cs;
@@ -323,6 +324,19 @@ bool PackedSourcePCK::try_open_pack(const String &p_path, bool p_replace_files,
                        PackedData::get_singleton()->remove_path(path);
                } else {
                        PackedData::get_singleton()->add_path(p_path, path, file_base + ofs, size, md5, this, p_replace_files, (flags & PACK_FILE_ENCRYPTED), sparse_bundle);
+                       if (flags & PACK_FILE_FORCE_RELOAD) {
+                               if (!path.begins_with("res://")) {
+                                       path = "res://" + path;
+                               }
+                               resources_to_reload.push_back(path);
+                       }
+               }
+       }
+
+       for (const String &path : resources_to_reload) { // After directory processing, to ensure all dependency files are loaded from patch pack.
+               Ref<Resource> res = ResourceCache::get_ref(path.trim_suffix(".import"));
+               if (res.is_valid()) {
+                       res->reload_from_file();
                }
        }
```
